                <pb facs="0804" n="706" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg706"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1628: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-11T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>862. Department infers that your No. 1143, July 29, 7 p.m. refers to the plan for
                    financing of Chinese Eastern Railway by consortium. Is that correct, and is
                    Department to understand that the French object to that proposal?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
